This follow-up was launched to answer the decisions the last run on this pull request left for the repository's owner. The launch carries that answer below, quoted as it was given: it is the launch's own text about those decisions, not a review instruction, and what it settles is what is listed under it and nothing else.

<<<fugaro-owner-ruling-0123456789abcdef>>>
    Counsel cleared the MIT text as it stands. Keep the approval flow.
<<<end-fugaro-owner-ruling-0123456789abcdef>>>

It answers these decisions, which that run left waiting:

    `LICENSE.md`: the licence text needs counsel's clearance
    `internal/approval/flow.go`: the approval flow is a product decision

A finding that is one of the decisions above is answered by that ruling: report it only if the change contradicts the answer, and never mark it needs_owner. Any other finding is reported as any finding is, and a new question only the owner can settle is still needs_owner, which is how the owner is asked about it.
